use crate::ai::gemini::GeminiClient;

pub const ARTICLE_CONTENT: &str = r#"Markets Brace for Crucial Global Economic Releases Date: January 26, 2026 Overview On January 26, 2026, global markets will closely monitor a series of high-impact economic indicators. Traders and investors are positioning themselves ahead of inflation prints, employment statistics, and policy updates, which are expected to provide direction for currency, equity, and fixed income markets. The collective data will be instrumental in shaping inflation expectations and monetary policy outlooks across major economies. Thematic Analysis Inflation Indicators Japan Tokyo Core CPI (YoY) (Jan): Forecast: 2.3%; Previous: 2.4%. As a key inflation gauge, this reading from Japan will influence JPY pairs and market views on Bank of Japan policy normalization. Australia Producer Price Index (QoQ) (Q4): Forecast: 1.2%; Previous: 1.2%. The PPI serves as an upstream inflation measure and will impact AUD volatility. Employment and Labor Data United States Initial Jobless Claims: Forecast: 215K; Previous: 212K. A crucial weekly update measuring trends in U.S. labor market resilience. Unexpected changes could influence Fed rate expectations. Germany Unemployment Change (Jan): Forecast: 7K; Previous: 8K. This key indicator for Europe’s largest economy will impact EUR sentiment. Growth and Industrial Production South Korea GDP (QoQ) (Q4): Forecast: 0.7%; Previous: 0.6%. As a bellwether for regional economic momentum, South Korea's economic performance can affect global risk appetite. Central Bank and Monetary Policy European Central Bank Interest Rate Decision: Forecast: 4.50%; Previous: 4.50%. The ECB is expected to maintain rates; forward guidance will be scrutinized for future policy shifts. Sentiment and PMI Data Germany Ifo Business Climate (Jan): Forecast: 87.0; Previous: 86.4. As a leading business sentiment barometer, the Ifo index will signal economic activity trends in the Eurozone. Commodities and Energy No high-impact releases scheduled for this sector. Other Relevant Releases Canada Wholesale Sales (MoM) (Dec): Forecast: 0.5%; Previous: 0.6%. While not typically market-moving, strong deviations may affect CAD volatility. Market Outlook Given the concentration of inflation and labor data, markets can expect increased volatility in major currency pairs, notably EUR/USD, USD/JPY, and AUD/USD. Equity and bond markets will react to any surprises in employment or inflation that shift expectations for global monetary policy. The ECB meeting stands out as a particular risk event for EUR instruments, especially if dovish or hawkish signals depart from consensus. Asian markets will be sensitive to South Korean GDP performance and Japanese inflation data. Conclusion from Myfxbook Analysts Myfxbook analysts highlight the European Central Bank decision, U.S. labor market data, and Japanese inflation figures as the primary high-volatility events for January 26, 2026. Market participants should prepare for swift price movements and potential breakouts in EUR, USD, and JPY crosses, with secondary attention to Australian and South Korean releases. Adherence to risk management strategies is recommended during this pivotal session."#;

pub async fn run_article_summary(api_key: String) -> Result<String, Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let client = GeminiClient::new(api_key);
    println!("Summarizing article in library module...");
    client.summarize(ARTICLE_CONTENT).await
}
